WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.020
Hey, Kinjiro. You serious about this?

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.660
Yeah, you can't stop me.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.870
Well, I didn't plan to stop you.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.490
Where will you go?

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.950
No idea. I haven't planned ahead.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.410
I am powerless to help

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.190
the people who come here with 
their wishes and concerns.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.870
And after decades and centuries 
of watching as time passes,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.880
I've grown tired.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.650
You need to take it easy.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.340
Let those humans say 
whatever they want.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.180
They don't believe in the gods,

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.670
and they can't see us.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.710
You're wrong.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.530
It's easier for them to 
be honest when speaking

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.820
to someone they can't see.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.310
Man, I'm guessing you've grown attached 
after watching humans so long,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.280
but there's not much point in 
wasting your time on humans.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.860
That's not how you truly feel, Gintaro.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.480
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.880
<b>The Place Where the Gods Are</b>

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.420
I've been thinking...

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:45.580
About what?

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.840
Why are you here?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.060
Am I not supposed to be?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.030
Now, now, now...

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.670
Oh, hey, Funabashi-san.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.240
Did you get in trouble 
for staying at my place?

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.470
No, nothing happened.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.950
I haven't talked to my 
mother since though.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.540
There's nothing for you to worry about.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.630
It wasn't your fault

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.670
and I feel much better now.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.330
Yeah, go wild.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.880
Oh, back to what I was saying.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.000
This is...

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.170
This is a map of modern Shinto City.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.350
This is a map of Shinto 
City in the Edo period.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.520
And?

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.680
You can see that there 
are castles, shrines,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.020
and temples which have survived.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.650
Including Saeki's home.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.530
Uh huh. Our shrine's been around since 
the beginning of the Edo period.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.240
When I visited your home, 
it made me think:

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.420
We all go to the same school and spend

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.710
most of our time together right now,

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:52.670
but once we graduate,
we'll go our separate ways.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:57.210
Yet, there are some 
things in our lives that

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.500
haven't changed in hundreds 
and thousands of years.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.630
Isn't that fascinating?

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.090
That's an interesting 
way to look at it.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.650
Huh? Really?

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.310
Our shrine started off as a small 
altar surrounded by farms.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.070
Every year, they would use the 
glowing lights of fox spirits

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.770
to divine how the upcoming 
year's harvest would fare.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.280
That was how it all began.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.940
In the Edo period, 
a feudal lord built the shrine

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:31.250
that's there now 
to increase the benefit.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.070
Inari is the god of agriculture.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.860
That's a fascinating story.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.130
That's right...

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.800
A lot of people have

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.920
made contributions to 
keeping our shrine alive.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.890
The tradition continues today.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.300
But castles and shrines aren't going to

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.200
remember the people 
who used to be around.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.640
Now, now, now...

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.150
Ishii, when did they get so friendly?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:02.190
The rumors about Funabashi 
and the student council president

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.650
have fizzled out, too.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.180
We totally embarrassed ourselves.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.680
Funabashi-san has interesting hobbies.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.550
Gin! Gintaro!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.140
Look! A turtle!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.320
It was heavy.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.010
I found it at the bottom of the stairs.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.530
It wasn't moving, 
so I brought it with me.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.290
Say, is Dad around?

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.800
Uh, Makoto?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.840
Oh. Welcome home, Makoto!

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.900
Look, Dad!

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.600
I found a turtle on the way home.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.280
Did it get lost?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.600
A turtle?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.490
Where is it?

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.030
Where is it?

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.200
Right here...

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.880
Fool, that's a herald.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.700
What?!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.470
Seriously...

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.850
You can't distinguish a herald 
from a normal turtle?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.220
That's sad...

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.600
Well, this is only the second 
herald I've ever met!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.510
Hey, wake up.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.620
Oh, he woke up.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.680
Wow, there are all kinds 
of different heralds.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.090
Of course.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.290
Lion-dogs are the most common,

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.700
since they're considered 
sacred animals.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:41.920
This is the first time I've 
ever spoken to a human.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.360
You didn't come from another shrine?

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.160
P-Pardon me...

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.930
Could I trouble you for some water?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.250
Oh, sure!

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.600
That hits the spot!

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:05.070
So why were you lying on the road?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.870
You see...

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:17.490
I lived in the small shrine by 
the lake beyond the mountains.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:22.090
But as time passed, our shrine

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:27.220
was forgotten and began to fall apart.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:34.870
Then, they tore up the lake 
and shrine to build new roads.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:40.160
I had no choice but to set off 
on a journey to find a new home.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.370
After a long and grueling trip, 
I was utterly exhausted.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.070
The lake he's talking about 
is just over in the next town.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.920
Well, he's just a turtle.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.530
Now that I have nowhere to go,

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:59.240
perhaps I should curse the 
humans who did this to me!

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.520
The thought crossed my mind,

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:07.800
but I don't have that kind 
of power, so I gave up.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.420
Plus, it would require effort.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.630
Yeah, a wise decision.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:20.060
Besides, the shrine was built for 
protection from drought and floods,

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:25.080
but now they say it's dangerous 
because kids will fall in the lake

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.440
Well, at least he's 
recovering sacred energy

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.080
while on the shrine grounds.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.290
Sacred energy?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:31.930
and the new road will make 
life easier for everybody.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.390
If a herald leaves his shrine 
for an extended period of time,

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.080
he'll lose his power.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.780
Oh...

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:38.560
Then you shouldn't have built 
the shrine in the first place!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.850
Well, we'll have to ask 
him to leave soon.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:36.870
Why?!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.410
This is an Inari shrine.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:44.580
When did humans turn into 
ungrateful monsters?

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.450
He's a herald for a different god.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.580
He won't be able to make 
a full recovery here.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:49.950
And dogs kept barking at me...

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.880
Are you listening to me?

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.130
Oh, a turtle herald?

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.830
That's amazing.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.350
Is he over there?

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.670
E-Er, who is this?

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.800
Oh, this is my dad.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.940
He's the chief priest here.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.650
I appreciate the hospitalit—

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.690
A turtle, huh?

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.110
I used to see a lot of turtles 
around when I was a child.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.190
You'd find them on roads near rivers.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:21.540
Whenever a car hit one, the shell 
would explode like fireworks.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.410
D-Dad!

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.740
Anyway, are there any shrines 
nearby with turtle heralds?

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.700
I believe that turtles would be found

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.970
at branches of the Matsunoo 
Grand Shrine in Kyoto, yes?

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.300
If you go past the station,

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.520
I believe you'll find Shoubai 
Grand Shrine which has a

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.770
Matsunoo altar in the back.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:46.340
Oh, that's the place 
with the lion-dogs.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.690
You know where it is, Gin?

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.480
I happened to be in the vicinity.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:54.250
Is it okay if we take you to a small 
altar instead of a full shrine?

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.700
I believe they have a lake there.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.310
Okay! Let's get going then!

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.260
It'll have to wait until tomorrow.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.620
The pain...

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.600
Um, are you okay, Mr. Turtle?

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.170
Is this better?

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.720
Yes, it feels wonderful.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.390
Seriously, this is one 
high maintenance turtle.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:30.670
O-Oh, I've been wondering...

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:34.270
Where is your partner?

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.400
His name is Kinjiro, right?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.700
You said he left a long time ago?

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.490
I-Is that so...

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:48.660
Gin, aren't you lonely 
without Kinjiro around?

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.360
Not really.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:53.530
Feels like it was just 
yesterday that he left.

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.380
I guess it's been a pretty long time.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.340
I completely forgot.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.800
I understand what you mean.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.660
When you live this long, 
your memory starts to go.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:10.270
I can't even remember what the 
weather was like yesterday.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.640
Um, I don't think that's 
quite the same...

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.390
Hey, Makoto!

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.280
The bath's ready for you!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.280
Okay!

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.910
Well... Good night, Mr. Turtle.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.270
Yes.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.990
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.870
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:31.590
Let's go, Gin.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.920
I have to come with you?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.290
He's pretty heavy.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:38.260
Come on. You can think of it as a date.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:43.700
S-Sorry about this.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.240
Then get off.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.430
Okay, let's go!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.350
Man, dates are a pain.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:56.820
The castle's still around?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.420
Any fond memories?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.400
No.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:03.570
I'm starting to understand what 
Funabashi-san meant, though.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:07.050
Some things in our 
lives have been there

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:10.000
for hundreds and thousands of years.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.410
Does it matter?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.710
A castle won't remember anything.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:17.690
<i>That's what Yumi-chan said.</i>

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:21.540
Come on, kitty. Over here.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.790
Hey, aren't we supposed 
to be catching a movie?!

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.040
Hey! You made it run away!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.020
You got plenty of petting time 
before we left my place.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.900
Isn't that fugly cat 
good enough for you?

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:39.190
You better not be giving 
Mi-chan a hard time.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:41.060
Why would I do that?!

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.520
Listen to this!

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:47.200
The other day, she came in my 
room and peed on my guitar!

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.940
I don't see a problem.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.290
You barely use it and never 
follow through with anything.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.460
What's that?!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.740
I'm sure you'll like the shrine.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:55.750
I hope the lake is clean.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:59.090
Oh, we'll come visit you 
once you've settled in.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.090
Saeki!

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.510
Yumi-chan?

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.510
Where are you headed?

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:08.800
I need to go to Shoubai Grand Shrine.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.590
Oh, there's a flea market 
there right now!

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:12.770
I'll come with you!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:13.580
Huh?

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.520
But...

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.440
What about your boyfriend?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.050
Um, Shouhei-kun?

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:22.000
Don't worry about him.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.450
I'm sure you don't want to go alone!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.260
Wow! It's so big!

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:35.080
Wait, you haven't been here before?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.060
I have, but it was when I was little...

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.660
Right, you live in a shrine.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.040
There are a lot of priests around.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.340
Wow, what a hottie!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:52.450
Can he see you, Gin?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:55.350
A true successor would 
be able to see me.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:58.030
Anyway, let's get this over with.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.020
Right...

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.330
Yumi-chan, I have some 
business to take care of,

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.680
so you can browse through 
the flea market.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.620
What's this? Something's up?

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.880
Are you hiding something from me?

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.490
I-I'm not hiding anything!

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.100
Mind your manners.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.870
Those monsters are over 
a thousand years old.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.260
R-Right...

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.680
There we go.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:26.990
Um, Gin?

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:28.730
What's got you so worried?

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:30.800
You told me to mind my manners.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:35.480
Hey! Are you geezers around?

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.260
Hello?

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.010
Who's there?

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.270
Keep it down.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.530
Lion-dogs!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.030
Good grief. Guess you're home.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.340
Oh, you're back again.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:57.850
Yo.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.540
Did you get in another 
fight with your priest?

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.290
I'm here for a different reason today.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.400
Has it been three days since 
we last spoke, Righty?

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.320
It's been seven days, Lefty.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.010
Really... Seven days...

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.130
Oof.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.270
Don't fall asleep!

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:20.600
Oh, my...

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:24.570
Oh, you are a priest?

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.530
This young girl is a priest?

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.950
Um, I'm not a priest yet...

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:38.390
It can't be easy to possess the 
Sight at such a young age.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:41.080
Plus, you're stuck with 
this fool of a fox.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:42.820
Who are you calling a fool?

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:45.150
E-Excuse me...

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.240
Oh?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:50.970
I-I have a request to make.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.940
Can you please help us?

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:58.140
Can you please let this turtle 
stay at the altar here?

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.520
Seriously, stop falling asleep.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.490
We don't see a problem with that.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:13.780
Make yourself at home.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:16.200
There's plenty of room.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.330
Thank you very much!

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.420
Isn't that great, Mr. Turtle?

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:26.270
Ow... I can't breathe...

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:37.240
How is it?

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:42.480
Yes, the altar is nearby 
and there's a lake.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.610
It doesn't get any better.

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:47.730
You're the ones 
who made it possible.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:48.900
I'm glad to hear that.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:55.860
I've recovered enough energy that 
I'm able to talk faster now.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.370
I don't see any change.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.780
Ah...

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:02.120
Well, I'll go look for Yumi-chan.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:02.740
Sure.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:06.240
Little girl! Little girl!

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:09.310
Righty and Lefty!

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:11.420
The turtle is thrilled 
about his new home.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:13.010
Thank you very much!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:15.190
That's good to hear,

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:19.470
but could you stop calling 
us Righty and Lefty?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.180
Those are nicknames we 
use for each other.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.020
Huh?

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:27.280
My actual name is Saimaru.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.900
I'm Utamaru.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.210
Saimaru-san and Utamaru-san.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.520
Those are cool names!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.480
You sound like traditional 
comical storytellers.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.570
Are you twins?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:39.970
No, I'm slightly older.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:44.460
In most cases, 
we're born without names.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.210
So I'm the one who named him.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.950
See the silly look on his face?

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:53.550
Yep, it's cute!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.360
You think he's cute?

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.900
That's not very respectful.

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:02.050
I'm starting to see why you 
and that fox had a spat.

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:02.850
Huh?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.560
Er.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.470
I-I'm sorry!

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:07.730
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.850
It's been a long time since we 
had a chance to talk to a human.

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.400
Thank you, little girl.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.530
O-Oh...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.700
I should thank you for 
welcoming the turtle.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.500
Er, wait...

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:22.230
The turtle spirit...

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.310
No need to thank us.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:26.820
My partner's the only person 
I've had to talk to,

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:30.630
so it'll be more fun 
with a new resident.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:35.620
When we were young, there were 
more humans who could see us,

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:37.980
but there aren't many these days.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:42.100
It's very rare to see 
a young one like you.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.600
What about the chief priest here?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.520
The chief priest is a true successor,

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:52.980
but his predecessor is still 
alive, so he can't see us.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:57.060
The prior chief priest has grown 
old and gone into retirement.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.700
He's very weak now.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.540
I didn't want to see 
that happen to him.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.690
Oh...

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:09.190
It may be hard for a young 
person like you to understand,

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:14.670
but when you live as long as we 
have, time flies by in a blink.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:19.610
The lifespan of a human is 
very brief in our eyes.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:24.990
We meet a priest one day and 
he dies before we even know it.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:31.380
We've experienced many 
farewells over the centuries.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:34.150
And as time goes on,

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:39.380
we can no longer remember the faces 
of the priests we were intimate with.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.480
It's rather sad.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:48.590
That fox may not want to admit it,

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:53.820
but he's enjoying his time with you.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:59.670
Gin, aren't you lonely 
without Kinjiro around?

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:01.380
Not really.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:04.350
Feels like it was just 
yesterday that he left.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.390
I guess it's been a pretty long time.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.350
I completely forgot.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.650
Hey!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.120
That's enough out of you guys.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.790
Oops!

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:23.480
Seriously, don't get carried away 
because you have a young girl to talk to.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.990
My apologies.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.490
Foxes have sharp ears.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.290
Let's go, Makoto.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.830
'Kay.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.480
Goodbye, Makoto-chan.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:37.270
Come visit us again.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.210
Uh huh, I'll be back!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:39.940
Bye!

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:04.960
Fool.

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:08.420
Don't believe what 
those lion-dogs said.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.250
That hurts.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:17.710
I'm going to die before you do.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.420
Yeah, that's expected.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:24.670
You must have ice in your veins,

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:27.650
since you'll forget 
about me in no time!

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:32.850
I couldn't forget about 
a stupid girl like you,

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:40.570
even if I wanted to.

00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.200
There you are!

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:03.840
<b>Shoubai Grand Shrine</b>

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:06.130
Jeez, where did you go?

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:07.320
Sorry.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.800
Anyway, I found a place 
with cute cat accessories!

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:12.700
More cat stuff?

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:12.700
Shut up!

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:13.850
This way!

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:20.990
Gin.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:24.110
Let's go! Our date's not over!

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:26.560
Hold on!

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:27.710
This way!

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:37.500
Yeah, dates are a pain.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:19.060
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:19.060
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:13.840
When you see a pair of 
lion-dogs at a shrine,

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:16.690
they typically have different faces.

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:19.060
Take a closer look next time.

00:24:19.140 --> 00:26:00.000
<b>Satoru and Haru</b>

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:21.850
Next time: "Satoru and Haru."

00:24:22.270 --> 00:24:24.450
May fortune be with you.
